			"value":[{
				"name":"the result",
				"type":"",
				"description":">*Note:*  On Mac OS systems, if the application is already running, the\n> <launch> command does nothing, and \"Process is already open.\" is\n> placed in the result function. On Windows and Linux, an additional\n> instance of the application will start."
			}],
			"description":"Use the <launch> <command> to start an application for the user to use.\n\nWhen the <launch> command executes, the application being launched comes\nto the foreground. When the user quits, OpenXTalk comes to the\nforeground. \n\nIf no <documentPath> is specified, the following two statements are\nequivalent: \n\n    launch application\n    open process application for neither\n\n>*Note:*  On OS X systems, you can use the <launch> command to start up\n> an application, but not a Unix process. To work with a Unix process,\n> use the shell function instead.\n\n>*Tip:*  On Windows systems, you can also start up an application by\n> using the shell function with the Windows \"start\" command:\n\n    get shell(\"start MyProgram.exe\")",
			"references":{
				"property":["hideConsoleWindows","secureMode"],
				"command":["launch url","kill","launch document"],
				"function":["shell"],
				"glossary":["command"]
			}
