			"value":[{
				"name":"the result",
				"type":"",
				"description":"If the sound playback could not be started, the command will return\n\"could not play sound\" in the <result>."
			}],
			"description":"Use the play file command to play a sound from a file.\n\nThe play file command will stop any currently playing sound, and then\nattempt to load the given sound file. If <looping> is specified the\nsound will repeat forever or until another sound is played.\n\nTo stop a sound that is currently playing use the command:\nplay empty\n\n>*Note:* Only one sound can be played at a time using the play file\n> command. \n\nThe volume at which a sound is played can be controlled using the\n<playLoudness> property. The overall volume of sound playback depends on\nthe current volume setting of the device.\n\nThis feature uses the built-in sound playback facilities in the iPhone\n(AVAudioPlayer) and Android and as such has support for a variety of\nformats. \n\n>*Cross-platform note:* This feature works the same way on bith Android\n> and iOS platforms, although the list of supported audio formats will\n> vary between devices.",
			"references":{
				"command":["play video","play","iphoneSetAudioCategory"],
				"function":["result","sound"],
				"property":["playLoudness"]
			},
			"tags":["multimedia"]
