			"description":"Load the text-to-speech software into memory when its needed by any of \nthe commands and functions in the <Speech library>.  The software\nshould be removed from memory when it is no longer needed by using the\n<revUnloadSpeech>.\n\n>*Important:*  The <revLoadSpeech> <command> is part of the \n> <Speech library>. To ensure that the <command> works in a \n> <standalone application>, you must include this \n> <OpenXTalk custom library|custom library> when you create your \n> <standalone application|standalone>. In the Inclusions pane of the \n> <Standalone Application Settings> window, make sure the \"Speech\" \n> library checkbox is checked.",
