			"description":"Use the <revPlayAnimation> <command> to display an animation that was\ncreated in the Animation Builder in older versions of OpenXTalk.\n\nAnimations were created using the Animation Builder, which was removed\nin OpenXTalk 2.5.\n\nThe <animationName> must be an animation that was created on the\n<current card> of the <defaultStack>.\n\nTo play a portion of the animation rather than the whole thing, specify\na <startFrame> and <endFrame> specifying the part of the animation you\nwant to play.\n\n>*Important:*  The <revPlayAnimation> <command> is part of the \n> <Animation library>. To ensure that the <command> works in a \n> <standalone application>, you must include this \n> <OpenXTalk custom library|custom library> when you create your \n> <standalone application|standalone>. In the Inclusions pane of the \n> <Standalone Application Settings> window, make sure the \"Animation\" \n> library checkbox is checked.",
