			"description":"The <revStopAnimation> command is no longer supported as the Animation\nBuilder was removed in version 2.5, however it is included for\nbackwards compatibility with older applications that used the Animation\nBuilder.\n\nUse the <revStopAnimation> <command> from within a <handler> that's\n<trigger|triggered> by a <key frame> to stop the current animation from\nplaying.\n\nAnimations were created using the Animation Builder in old versions.\nThe Animation builder is no longer available.\n\nThe <animationName> must be an animation that was created on the\n<current card> of the <defaultStack>.\n\n>*Important:*  The <revStopAnimation> <command> is part of the\n> <Animation library>. To ensure that the <command> works in a\n> <standalone application>, you must include this\n> <OpenXTalk custom library|custom library> when you create your\n> <standalone application|standalone>. In the Inclusions pane of the\n> <Standalone Application Settings> window, make sure the \"Animation\"\n> library checkbox is checked.",
