			"description":"Use the <ln> function to obtain a base e logarithm.\n\nThe natural logarithm of a <number> is the power to which e must be\nraised to obtain the <number>.\n\nThe transcendental number e appears in many mathematical formulas.\n\nTo find the logarithm of a number in any base, use the following\nfunction: \n\n    function logarithm theBase,theNumber\n        return ln(theNumber)/ln(theBase)\n    end logarithm\n\nIf a math operation on finite inputs produces a non-finite output, an\nexecution error is thrown. See <math operation|math operations> for more\ninformation.",
