			"description":"Use the <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> <function> to make <XML> text\ninto an <XML tree> which returns XML namespace tags and attributes as\npart of the tree without doing any processing.\n\nUse the <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> function to make XML Text into\nan XML Tree, ignoring XML Namespace related tags and functions. The\n<revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> function returns namespace tags and\nattributes as part of the tree without doing any processing.\n\nUse the <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> function when an application\nneeds the namespace information to perform correctly.\n\nIf the <dontparseBadData> is false, the <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces>\n<function> tries to parse <XML> data even if it is not well-formed.\nOtherwise, the <function> stops executing as soon as it encounters data\nthat is not well-formed <XML>.\n\nIf the <createTree> is true, the <function> creates a tree structure in\nmemory. Otherwise, the <function> simply parses the <XML> data without\ncreating an <XML tree>.\n\nIf the <sendMessages> is true, the <revXMLStartTree>, <revStartXMLNode>,\n<revStartXMLData>, <revEndXMLNode>, and <revXMLEndTree>\n<message|messages> are sent while the <XML> data is being parsed.\nOtherwise, these <message|messages> are not sent.\n\nIf the <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> <function> encounters an error,\nit <return|returns> an error message starting with \"xmlerr\".\n\n>*Important:*  The <revXMLCreateTreeWithNamespaces> <function> is part\n> of the\n> <XML library>. To ensure that the <function> works in a \n> <standalone application>, you must include this \n> <OpenXTalk custom library|custom library> when you create your \n> <standalone application|standalone>. In the Inclusions pane of the \n> <Standalone Application Settings> window, make sure the \"XML\" \n> checkbox is checked.",
