			"description":"Use the <selectedText> <function> to find out what text is <selected>.\n\nIf a <field> is specified, the <selectedText> <function>\n<return|returns> the <selected> text in that <field(keyword)>. If the\n<field(object)|field's> <listBehavior> <property> is set to true, the\n<selectedText> includes any <selected> <lines> in the <field(keyword)>.\n\nIf a <button> is specified, the <selectedText> <function>\n<return|returns> the currently <selected> <menu item> associated with\nthe <button>. If the <button> does not have a <menu> associated with it,\nthe <selectedText> <function> <return|returns> empty.\n\nIf there is no insertion point or text selection and no <field> or\n<button> is specified, the <selectedText> <function> <return|returns>\nempty. \n\nTo get the location of the selected text, use the selectedChunk\n<function>. \n\nTo change the contents of the selection, use the <selection> <keyword>.",
