			"description":"Use the <any> <keyword> to specify a <random(glossary)>\n<object(glossary)> of a specified type, or to designate a\n<random(glossary)> <chunk> in a <chunk expression>.\n\nThe <any> <keyword> does not examine every member of a set; it specifies\njust one member of the set, randomly chosen. For example, the expression\n\n    if myString is in any field\n\nchecks whether `myString` is in a randomly chosen field, not whether\n`myString` is somewhere in one of the fields on the card.",
