			"description":"Use the <modem:> <keyword> to communicate through the modem serial\n<port>. \n\nTo set the port parameters (such as baud rate, handshaking, and parity),\nset the <serialControlString> <property> before opening the <port> with\nthe <open file> <command>.\n\nTo read data from the modem port, use the <read from file> command,\nspecifying the keyword modem: as the file to read from.\n\nTo write data to the modem port, use the <write to file> <command>.\n\nTo use the printer port on Mac OS systems, use the printer: <keyword>.\n(To use serial ports other than the built-in printer or modem port, use\nthe <open driver> <command>.)\n\nTo use serial ports on Windows systems, use the <COMn:|COM1:> through \n<COMn:|COM9:> <keyword|keywords>. ",
