			"type":"keyword",
			"syntax":[
				"rectangle"
			],
			"display syntax":[
				"rectangle"
			],
			"synonyms":["rect"],
			"summary":"Specifies that a <button(object)>, <field>, or <graphic>\n<object(glossary)> is shaped like a rectangle. It also designates the\n<paint tool> used to draw rectangles and squares.",
			"introduced":"1.0",
			"OS":["mac","windows","linux","ios","android"],
			"platforms":["desktop","server","mobile"],
			"examples":[{
				"script":"choose rectangle tool"
			},{
				"script":"set the style of button ID 3 to rectangle"
			}],
			"description":"Use the <rectangle> <keyword> to paint a rectangle or square with the\n<penColor> or to change a <graphic(keyword)> to a rectangle shape.\n\nWhen using the Rectangle tool, the cursor is a crosshairs shape (over\nstack windows) or an arrow (anywhere else). This tool is used to draw a\nrectangle or square in the penColor, filled with the <brushColor> (or\n<brushPattern>). \n\nIf you try to paint with the Rectangle tool on a card that has no\nimages, an image the size of the card is created to hold the painting.\nIf the current card already has one or more images, painting outside the\nimage has no effect.\n\nSetting the style of a <graphic(keyword)> to rectangle makes the graphic\ninto a rectangle. Rectangle <graphic(object)|graphics>, unlike painted\nrectangles, can be changed and reshaped: use the <height> and <width>\n<properties> to change the shape and size of the rectangle.\n\nSetting the style of a <field> or <button> to rectangle <a/>makes it a\nrectangle shape.",
			"references":{
				"keyword":["field","graphic"],
				"property":["width","brushColor","height","properties","penColor","brushPattern"],
				"command":["choose"],
				"object":["button","graphic"],
				"glossary":["object","keyword","paint tool"]
			},
			"tags":["ui"]
