			"description":"Use the <templateAudioClip> <keyword> to set up <default> <properties>\nto be used for any new <audio clip|audio clips> you create.\n\nThe <templateAudioClip> can be thought of as a special, abstract\n<object(glossary)>. It is not an actual <audio clip>, but it has all the\n<properties> of an <audio clip>. The <ID> <property> of the\n<templateAudioClip> is zero.\n\nYou can use the <set> <command> to set the <properties> of the\n<templateAudioClip> before creating an <audio clip>. The new \n<audio clip> has the <properties> of the <templateAudioClip>, by <default>.\nChanging the <properties> of the <templateAudioClip> does not affect\nexisting <audio clip|audio clips>.\n\nThe properties of the <templateAudioClip> can be returned to the default\nsettings using the <reset> command.\n\nYou can refer to the <templateAudioClip> using any of the following\nforms:templateAudioClip\n\n    the templateAudioClip\n    templateAudioClip()\n\n\n>*Note:* The <templateAudioClip> <keyword> is implemented internally as\n> a <function> and appears in the <functionNames>. However, it cannot be\n> used as a <function> in an <expression>.",
