			"summary":"Sent to the <current card> when you go from a <card> that does not have\na <group> to a <card> that does.",
			"introduced":"1.0",
			"OS":["mac","windows","linux","ios","android"],
			"platforms":["desktop","server","mobile"],
			"parameters":[{
				"name":"pBackgroundID",
				"type":"",
				"refparam":"false",
				"description":"The short ID property of the background being opened."
			}],
			"examples":[{
				"script":"on preOpenBackground theGroup -- move the group's position\n  if the short name of background ID theGroup is \"Navigation\"\n  then set the bottom of group \"Navigation\" to the height of this card\nend preOpenBackground"
			}],
			"description":"Handle the <preOpenBackground> <message> to update a\n<background|background's> appearance before the <background> appears on\nscreen. \n\nThe actual navigation is not triggered by the <preOpenBackground>\n<message>, so <trap|trapping> the <message> and not allowing it to\n<pass> does not prevent the <card> with the <group> from opening. For\neach <group> on the card that was not on the previously visited card, a\n<preOpenBackground> <message> (with the group ID) is sent to the current\ncard. If the card does not handle the message, or passes it, the message\nproceeds through each group in reverse layer order (from highest to\nlowest). Each <group> which handles the <message> should be careful to\ncheck that the ID matches itself to prevent inadvertantly trappng a\nmessage intended for a different group.",
