			"description":"Use the <bitOr> <operator> to operate directly on the <bit|bits> of two\nnumbers. \n\nTo perform the <bitOr> <operation>, OpenXTalk first converts both\n<operand|operands> to their <binary> equivalent, a string of ones and\nzeroes. 1 is equivalent to true, and 0 is equivalent to false.\n\nFor each bit of <number1>, OpenXTalk performs an <or> <operation> with\nthe corresponding <bit> of <number2> to produce a result. A <bit> is 0\nif the corresponding <bit|bits> of <number1> and <number2> are both 0.\nOtherwise, the <bit> is 1.\n\nFinally, the binary number thus created is converted back to decimal.",
