			"description":"Use the <bitXOr> <operator> to operate directly on the <bit|bits> of two\nnumbers. \n\nTo perform the <bitXOr> <operation>, OpenXTalk first converts both\n<operand|operands> to their <binary> equivalent, a string of ones and\nzeroes. 1 is equivalent to true, and 0 is equivalent to false.\n\nFor each bit of <number1>, OpenXTalk performs an exclusive <or>\n<operation> with the corresponding <bit> of <number2> to produce a\nresult. A <bit> is 0 if the corresponding <bit|bits> of <number1> and\n<number2> are both 0 or both 1. Otherwise, the <bit> is 1.\n\nFinally, the binary number thus created is converted back to decimal.",
