			"description":"Use the <bottomRight> <property> to change the placement of a <control>\nor window.\n\nThe <bottomRight> of a <stack> is in \n<absolute coordinates(glossary)|absolute (screen) coordinates>. \nThe first <item> (the <right>) of a\n<card|card's> <bottomRight> <property> is always the width of the \n<stack window>; the second <item> (the <bottom>) is always the height\nof the <stack window>. The <bottomRight> of a <group> or <control> is\nin <relative coordinates(glossary)|relative (window) coordinates>.\n\nIn window coordinates, the point 0,0 is at the top left of the stack\nwindow. In screen coordinates, the point 0,0 is at the top left of the\nscreen. \n\nChanging the <bottomRight> of an <object(glossary)> moves it to the new\nposition without resizing it. To change an <object|object's> size, set\nits <height>, <width>, or <rectangle> <properties>.\n\n>*Important:*  The order of the bottom and right <parameter|parameters>\n> is reversed compared to the <property> name: right comes first, then\n> bottom. ",
