			"value":[{
				"name":"value",
				"type":"",
				"description":"The <linkHiliteColor> is a <color reference>.\nA <colorName> is any standard color name.\n\nAn <RGBColor> consists of three comma-separated <integer|integers>\nbetween zero and 255, specifying the level of each of red, green, and\nblue; or an HTML-style color consisting of a hash mark (#) followed by\nthree <hexadecimal> numbers, one for each of red, green, and blue.\n\nBy default, the <linkHiliteColor> is set to \"255,0,0\" (bright red). The\n<linkHiliteColor> of a newly created <stack> is set to empty by\n<default>. "
			}],
			"description":"Use the <linkHiliteColor> <property> to make <grouped text> look and\nbehave like links in a <browser|web browser>.\n\nThe <linkHiliteColor> appears to show that <grouped text> is being\nclicked. When the <mouse button> is released, the text color changes to\nthe <linkVisitedColor>.\n\nIf the <linkHiliteColor> of a <stack> is empty, <grouped text> in that\n<stack> is shown with the <global> <linkHiliteColor> <property> when\nbeing clicked.\n\nIf the <linkHiliteColor> of a <stack> is not empty, <grouped text> in\nthat <stack> is shown with the <stack|stack's> <linkHiliteColor>\n<property>, regardless of the <global> setting.",
