			"associations":["group"],
			"summary":"Specifies whether clicking an <object(glossary)> in a <group>\n<select|selects> the <object(glossary)> or the entire <group>.",
			"introduced":"1.0",
			"OS":["mac","windows","linux","ios","android"],
			"platforms":["desktop","server","mobile"],
			"examples":[{
				"script":"set the selectGroupedControls to (not the selectGroupedControls)"
			}],
			"description":"Use the <selectGroupedControls> <property> to control what happens when\nyou click a <grouped control>.\n\nIf the <selectGroupedControls> <property> is set to false, clicking an\n<object(glossary)> in a <group> with the <Pointer tool>\n<select(glossary)|selects> the entire <group>. You must set the\n<editBackground> <property> to true to in order <select(command)>, move,\nresize, and change individual <object|objects> in the <group>.\n\nIf the <selectGroupedControls> is true, clicking an <object(glossary)>\nin a <group> <select(glossary)|selects> only that <object(glossary)>,\neven if the <editBackground> is false.\n\nYou can change the <selectGroupedControls> <property> by choosing Edit →\nSelect Grouped Controls from the menubar.",
