			"description":"Use the <textShift> <property> to subscript and superscript\n<chunk|chunks> of text in a <field(keyword)>.\n\nThe <textShift> is the number of <pixels> to shift the text down from\nthe baseline, creating a subscript. If the <textShift> is <negative>,\nthe text is shifted up (superscripted). If the <textShift> is zero, the\ntext is placed in normal position, not shifted up or down.\n\n>*Note:* If the <field(object)|field's> <fixedLineHeight> <property> is\n> true, you may need to increase the <field(object)|field's>\n> <textHeight> to make room for subscripts and superscripts.",
