			"display syntax":[
				"set the unboundedVScroll of <i>group</i> to {true | false}"
			],
			"associations":["group"],
			"summary":"Specifies whether automatic clamping of the vScroll offsets of a group\nis on or off.",
			"introduced":"4.6",
			"OS":["mac","windows","linux","ios","android"],
			"platforms":["desktop","server"],
			"examples":[{
				"script":"set the unboundedVScroll of group \"items\" to true"
			}],
			"description":"Use the <unboundedVScroll> property to turn automatic clamping of the\n<vScroll> offset of a group on or off.\n\nWhen the <unboundedVScroll> property of a <group> is set to true and the\n<vScrollbar> is not visible, it is possible to set the <vScroll>\nproperty of the <group> to values outside that of the size of the\ncontent (both positive and negative).\n\nIf the <vScrollbar> of the <group> is made visible or the\n<unboundedVScroll> property is turned off and the <vScroll> value is\noutside of the content bounds, the <group> is scrolled to bring the\n<vScroll> value within the appropriate range.",
